<title>FRANCE: SOCCER-FRANCE AND BRAZIL DRAW 1-1 IN TOURNOI DE FRANCE.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-FRANCE AND BRAZIL DRAW 1-1 IN TOURNOI DE FRANCE.</headline>
<dateline>LYON, France 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>France and Brazil drew 1-1 (halftime 0-1) in their Tournoi de France international soccer match on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>France - Marc Keller 60</p>
<p>Brazil - Roberto Carlos 21</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>France - 16-Fabien Barthez; 2-Vincent Candela, 5-Laurent Blanc, 8-Marcel Desailly (15-Lilian Thuram 67), 12-Bixente Lizarazu; 13-Ibrahim Ba, 19-Christian Karembeu (17-Patrick Vieira 14), 7-Didier Deschamps, 10-Zinedine Zidane; 22-Florian Maurice, 14-Robert Pires (21-Marc Keller 46)</p>
<p>Brazil - 1-Taffarel; 2-Cafu, 15-Celio Silva, 3-Aldair (16-Goncalves 88), 6-Roberto Carlos; 7-Giovanni (13-Djalminha 72), 5-Mauro Silva, 8-Dunga, 10-Leonardo; 9-Ronaldo, 11-Romario (22-Paulo Nunes 79)</p>
<p>Referee: Kim Milton Nielsen (Denmark)</p>
